Subject: [PATCH] Discover Qualcomm Venus stateful decoders

Local change against libva-v4l2 v1.0.0:
https://github.com/radxa-pkg/libva-v4l2/tree/0e4ce1e05da1d0a92b342efc2090b9e4987035e1

Venus provides the decode-order controls and DMA-BUF capture used by this
backend. Accept its driver name while retaining the M2M and compressed OUTPUT
format checks, so camera and encoder nodes are not selected. Video indices
can change between boots.

On SDM845 Polaris with Linux 7.3-rc5, stock FFmpeg VA-API H264 High and HEVC
Main each pass 90 frames with B frames and pixel-exact software comparisons.
Do not extend encoder discovery: Venus encoding still faults in firmware.

--- a/src/decoder.cpp
+++ b/src/decoder.cpp
@@ -72,7 +72,8 @@
         v4l2_capability cap{};
         bool match = false;
         if (!call(fd, VIDIOC_QUERYCAP, &cap) &&
-            !strcmp(reinterpret_cast<char *>(cap.driver), "iris_driver")) {
+            (!strcmp(reinterpret_cast<char *>(cap.driver), "iris_driver") ||
+             !strcmp(reinterpret_cast<char *>(cap.driver), "qcom-venus"))) {
             unsigned caps =
                 cap.capabilities & V4L2_CAP_DEVICE_CAPS ? cap.device_caps : cap.capabilities;
             if (caps & V4L2_CAP_VIDEO_M2M_MPLANE) {
@@ -89,7 +90,7 @@
         if (match)
             return path;
     }
-    throw Error(VA_STATUS_ERROR_OPERATION_FAILED, "no Iris stateful H264 decoder found");
+    throw Error(VA_STATUS_ERROR_OPERATION_FAILED, "no Qualcomm stateful H264 decoder found");
 }
 bool device_supports_av1(const std::string &device) {
     int fd = open(device.c_str(), O_RDWR | O_NONBLOCK | O_CLOEXEC);
